; The monastery. All static geometry, all on collision layer 1 (world).
;
; Footprints (x, z), ground level y = 0:
;   Church nave    x  -9..9    z -34..-12   walls 7m, door gap x -2..2
;   Side building  x  16..30   z -28..-16   walls 4m, door gap z -23..-21
;   Low wall       x -40..40   z -44..14    1.6m, gate gap x -3..3
;   Crypt          x  -2..16   z -24..-4    floor at y = -4.5
;   Stairwell      x   6..12   z  -4..6     descends 0 -> -4.5
;
; STAIRS: the collision is ONE smooth tilted box; the nine visible steps are
; MeshInstance3D only, with no collision at all. Godot's CharacterBody3D has no
; built-in step-up, so a capsule cannot climb 0.5m boxes -- it just wedges. The
; standard greybox answer is to let the player walk an invisible ramp while the
; eye sees stairs. If you ever add real step-up logic to PlayerMotor, swap the
; ramp shape out for per-step shapes.
